From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:22:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: add a compat/unsafe build profile for the defaults of
 trade-off switches

Some switches trade valid but rarely used Vulkan behaviour for memory or
speed. They stay off by default, so a build that should have them on
needed an environment variable per game.

New meson option panvk-profile (compat or unsafe, default compat). It sets
PANVK_PROFILE_UNSAFE, the compiled-in default of such switches; the
environment variable still overrides it per process in either build.
driverInfo names the profile ("PanVK-kbase RC3-lowmem unsafe (Mesa ...)").

compat: every default is conformant (PanProbe 38/38).
unsafe: also PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW (rg477m/020): BC images on the fragment-decode
path keep no raw blocks, 25-50% less texture memory; reading the blocks
back is skipped with a warning, so PanProbe's bc_decode raw-readback check
fails (37/38).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: build profiles: meson option panvk-profile=compat|unsafe sets the compiled-in default of switches that trade conformance for memory or speed (unsafe: PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW on); env variables still override per process; driverInfo names the profile. Fork scripts/build-android.sh passes it with --panvk-profile
Upstream-commit: none (fork build option)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/020 (PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW); applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/021
Validation test: PanProbe compat 38/38 x2, unsafe 37/38 x2 (only bc_decode raw readback fails, by design); bcsize 2048x2048 BC1/BC3 per build and env: compat 8.0/16.0 MiB, compat PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW=1 5.3/10.7, unsafe 5.3/10.7, unsafe PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW=0 8.0/16.0; driverInfo "PanVK-kbase RC3-lowmem compat|unsafe (Mesa ...)"; Arkham Asylum (32-bit, rg477m/021 path active) on unsafe (then named fast): 3/3 to gameplay with a checkpoint reload, no specks, 0 GPU faults, 25.0-26.7 fps; Arkham converts its textures to ASTC in GameNative, so 020 is inactive there
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 meson.options                                  | 11 +++++++++++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build                |  2 ++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c              |  6 +++---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c |  4 ++--
 4 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.options b/meson.options
index 36e090cc..8f6cd44c 100644
--- a/meson.options
+++ b/meson.options
@@ -236,6 +236,17 @@ option(
                 'gallium and vulkan driver',
 )
 
+option(
+  'panvk-profile',
+  type : 'combo',
+  value : 'compat',
+  choices : ['compat', 'unsafe'],
+  description : 'Compiled-in defaults of PanVK-kbase switches. compat: only ' +
+                'conformant behaviour. unsafe: also enables tested trade-offs ' +
+                'that break rarely used valid Vulkan (each switch can still ' +
+                'be set per process with its environment variable).',
+)
+
 option(
   'amdgpu-virtio',
   type : 'boolean',
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build b/src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build
index 437a8e73..79dc340a 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -70,6 +70,8 @@ libpanvk_files += [sha1_h]
 
 panvk_deps = []
 panvk_flags = []
+# compat or unsafe: the compiled-in default of switches that trade conformance for memory or speed
+panvk_flags += '-DPANVK_PROFILE_UNSAFE=@0@'.format(get_option('panvk-profile') == 'unsafe' ? 1 : 0)
 panvk_per_arch_libs = []
 
 bifrost_archs = [6, 7]
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
index 1eb7e2eb..11aeb429 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
@@ -772,10 +772,10 @@ panvk_image_init(struct panvk_image *image,
                    pan_arch(phys_dev->kmod.dev->props.gpu_id) >= 10 &&
                    image->vk.image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D &&
                    !PANVK_DEBUG(BC_COMPUTE) && !PANVK_DEBUG(NO_GS);
-   /* Opt-in (PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW=1): reading the blocks back breaks, so it stays off by default. Images the app may
-    * view or map as raw blocks keep them. */
+   /* PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW: reading the blocks back breaks, so it is off by default except in the unsafe build profile.
+    * Images the app may view or map as raw blocks keep them. */
    image->bc_noraw =
-      image->bc_gfx && debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW", false) &&
+      image->bc_gfx && debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_BC_DROP_RAW", PANVK_PROFILE_UNSAFE) &&
       pCreateInfo->tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL &&
       !(pCreateInfo->flags & (VK_IMAGE_CREATE_BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE_BIT |
                               VK_IMAGE_CREATE_SPARSE_BINDING_BIT |
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
index 802118c7..6193b467 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -1392,8 +1392,8 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_properties)(
 
    snprintf(properties->driverName, VK_MAX_DRIVER_NAME_SIZE, "panvk");
    snprintf(properties->driverInfo, VK_MAX_DRIVER_INFO_SIZE,
-            "PanVK-kbase " PANVK_KBASE_RELEASE " (Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION
-            MESA_GIT_SHA1 ")");
+            "PanVK-kbase " PANVK_KBASE_RELEASE " %s (Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION
+            MESA_GIT_SHA1 ")", PANVK_PROFILE_UNSAFE ? "unsafe" : "compat");
 
    /* VK_EXT_physical_device_drm */
    if (device->drm.primary_rdev) {
